  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 134 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nHot and generally dry weather continues through the Long Term as the \nridge continues to slide westward and eventually builds over the \nFour Corners region. Highs Friday look similar Thursday's overall, \nand an additional Heat Advisory may be deemed necessary in future \nforecast updates. This weekend, thicknesses over our area decrease \nslightly as the ridge sets up over the Four Corners, so temperatures \ntick down a degree or two relative to Thursday and Friday. That \nbeing said, most locations still top out in the upper 90s and \nat/just above 100 degrees Saturday and Sunday (low-to-mid 90s in and \nnear the higher terrain). By early next week, temperatures start to \ntrend back up as the ridge begins to gradually shift eastward again. \nFor most locations, rain chances through the extended forecast are \nnil. That being said, occasional showers and storms will be possible \nin the higher terrain. Models also depict showers and thunderstorms \ndeveloping in southeast New Mexico Friday and perhaps again Saturday \nthanks to subtle disturbances in the flow aloft. However, chances \nremain low (10-20%) at this time.\n\nSprang",
